                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10683d82-d3ac-38ee-b89e-6383815e9fe0",
                        "entry_id": "a7700e5e-304f-3cc7-bc7a-b22ae28039e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "биохим., генет. фосфорный эфир нуклеозида, мономер нуклеиновых кислот"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc29c859-7dec-4ed9-a66e-d917135b297d",
                                "sense_id": "10683d82-d3ac-38ee-b89e-6383815e9fe0",
                                "text": "Задача, стоящая перед рибосомой, очень сложная. Ведь белки состоят не из нуклеотидов, а из принципиально других строительных блоков ― аминокислот. Причём нуклеотидов всего четыре, а аминокислот ― двадцать."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce0c5233-40a8-482e-9707-2a5fa1e8bfe2",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7700e5e-304f-3cc7-bc7a-b22ae28039e5",
                        "source_sense_id": "10683d82-d3ac-38ee-b89e-6383815e9fe0",
                        "target_lang_word": "nucleotide",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nucleotide",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff3d126f-dff2-3fea-a638-abcd7b17071c",
                                        "entry_id": "a2990c6e-69ff-37e4-b4af-ecd18beaad40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The monomer constituting DNA or RNA biopolymer molecules. Each nucleotide consists of a nitrogenous heterocyclic base (or nucleobase), which can be either a double-ringed purine or a single-ringed pyrimidine; a five-carbon pentose sugar (deoxyribose in DNA or ribose in RNA); and a phosphate group."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7d37f79-32d0-498a-b4f4-5a3f2a9f1abc",
                                                "sense_id": "ff3d126f-dff2-3fea-a638-abcd7b17071c",
                                                "text": "With a genome of only 400 million or so nucleotide bases, the pufferfish, Fugu rubripes rubripes, has the smallest known genome of any vertebrate animal. […] But the region of DNA between the landmarks can be a million or more nucleotides long."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1666e13-1869-4af2-9c16-9e00332b2700",
                                                "sense_id": "ff3d126f-dff2-3fea-a638-abcd7b17071c",
                                                "text": "Magid draws […] a diagram depicting a restriction enzyme cutting neatly through a sequence of nucleotides."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
